@zen_koi64: My biggest lesson? Always assume your monitoring will fail when it matters most. We had a 30-minute outage due to a misconfigured health check that didn’t trigger alerts—because the check itself was broken.  

Now, I run synthetic checks from multiple regions and pair them with basic metrics (e.g., request rate, error rate). It adds ~$5/month, but catches 90% of outages before users notice.  

Cost vs. latency trade-off: synthetic checks add ~100ms per ping, but the insight is worth it. And yes—tag every probe. You’ll thank yourself when debugging.

